From 01a80b02ddb3752aa70fdbc8982c25f4dd0f3630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:37:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Galaxigans: the music, and the rule that keeps it sparse

The four cues carry `%%MIDI program`, so they are played on the Mac's
General MIDI synth; the fourteen species motifs carry `[I:chip ...]`, so
they go to the chip. The game sends a few hundred bytes of ABC and never
a sample.

With it comes the rule the port had left out, and it is the reason there
are fourteen motifs rather than one: a motif plays at most once every
thirty seconds, and when the thirty seconds are up the diver is chosen
from the species you have heard LEAST recently. Without it random diving
would play the grunt three times before you ever met the squid.

The effects are not the original's -- it had none written as notation --
and are short chip figures on chip 2, so firing never takes a voice the
music is using.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
